 "description": "Showtimes scoped by FILM or by THEATER on one board \u2014 pass at least one. With `film`: where that film is playing (title or slug; fuzzy-matched, ambiguous queries return candidates). With `venues` and no film: everything on at those theaters, each showtime naming its film. Grouped by theater with local times, tags (35mm/qa/sold-out), the night each show belongs to, and a ticket link per showtime. Optional date and time-window filters apply to both. Returns the 40 nearest showtimes (\"concise\") or up to 200 (\"detailed\"); showtime_count is the total and showtimes_complete says whether the list is whole, so narrow by date or theater for the rest. For the whole board with no film or theater in mind, call scenef_whats_playing instead. Read-only: the call itself records nothing. SceneF does not sell, hold or book tickets. Ticket links are https://scenef.com/go/{id} redirects to the theater's own site or the ticket seller it uses (a link to a showtime that is gone lands back on SceneF); whoever follows one, a person or a client, is logged once anonymously (time, the screening with its film and theater, client type, browser family, referring site, link source tag, and whether the showtime was gone; no IP address, cookie or account) and forwarded. Every emitted showtime carries confidence, source tier, reporting sources and verified_at.",
 "inputSchema": {
  "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
  "properties": {
   "date": {
    "description": "Restrict to one night, YYYY-MM-DD.",
    "maxLength": 120,
    "type": "string"
   },
   "film": {
    "description": "Film title, or a SceneF slug taken from films[].slug / scenef_whats_playing. A title that is not on the board answers with a miss and points at scenef_whats_playing, so guessing is safe but browsing is faster. Optional when `venues` is given \u2014 omit it to ask what is on at a theater.",
    "maxLength": 120,
    "type": "string"
   },
   "region": {
    "description": "Which regional board to read: a board id such as \"sf\", \"oahu\" or \"miami\", not a city name (\"Honolulu\" or \"Chicago\" is rejected). Omitted means \"sf\" (San Francisco); it is never inferred from where you are. For a city, ZIP or neighborhood call scenef_resolve_board first; scenef_now with no region lists every id. An unknown region is an error, not a fallback.",
    "maxLength": 120,
    "type": "string"
   },
   "response_format": {
    "description": "Output size. \"concise\" (default) is tight text plus a structured summary. In whats_playing, each film has the total showtime_count, next_showtime, and a showtimes array containing only that next screening; \"detailed\" adds showtime rows with ids, ticket urls and accuracy metadata, about 200 across the answer. film_details and search_showtimes return the 40 nearest showtimes in \"concise\" and up to 200 in \"detailed\". showtime_count is always the total and showtimes_complete says whether the array is all of it; narrow by date or theater for the rest.",
    "enum": [
     "concise",
     "detailed"
    ],
    "type": "string"
   },
   "time_after": {
    "description": "Only shows at or after this local time, \"HH:MM\" 24h.",
    "maxLength": 120,
    "type": "string"
   },
   "time_before": {
    "description": "Only shows at or before this local time, \"HH:MM\" 24h.",
    "maxLength": 120,
    "type": "string"
   },
   "venues": {
    "description": "Restrict to these theaters (ids or names), e.g. [\"roxie\", \"Balboa\"]. Required when `film` is omitted.",
    "items": {
     "maxLength": 80,
     "type": "string"
    },
    "maxItems": 10,
    "type": "array"
   }
  },
  "type": "object"
 },
